\title{geevis: Google Earth Engine, Satellite and Drone Imagery, and Vegetation Indices}
\description{
Tools to go from imagery to plot-level tables of bands and vegetation indices. Sets up the Python environment and authentication that 'rgee' needs for Google Earth Engine, downloads and summarises satellite bands and vegetation indices over polygon regions and phenological phases, extracts the same from local (e.g. drone) rasters with optional vegetation segmentation by Otsu, triangle or k-means thresholds, merges overlapping rasters, and ships a built-in table of vegetation index equations. Includes a trilingual (Portuguese, English, Spanish) cheat sheet, gee_tips().
}
